================================================================================
                               TMUX CHEAT SHEET
================================================================================

1. TERMINAL COMMANDS (OUTSIDE TMUX)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmux                                Start a new unnamed session[cite: 1]
tmux new -s <name>                  Create a new session with a name[cite: 1]
tmux ls                             List all running sessions[cite: 1]
tmux attach -t <name>               Attach to a specific session (short: tmux a -t <name>)[cite: 1]
tmux attach                         Attach to the last used session (short: tmux a)[cite: 1]
tmux switch-client -t <name>        Switch to another session from terminal[cite: 1]
tmux rename-session -t <old> <new>  Rename a session[cite: 1]
tmux kill-session -t <name>         Kill/delete a specific session[cite: 1]
tmux kill-server                    Kill all sessions and stop tmux server[cite: 1]


2. SESSION SHORTCUTS (INSIDE TMUX)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ctrl+B then D                       Detach from current session[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then S                       Show session list (select with Up/Down -> Enter)[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then (                       Switch to previous session[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then )                       Switch to next session[cite: 1]


3. WINDOW SHORTCUTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ctrl+B then C                       Create a new window[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then N                       Go to next window[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then P                       Go to previous window[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then <number>                Go to window number (e.g. 0, 1, 2)[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then W                       List all windows interactively[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then ,                       Rename current window[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then &                       Close current window[cite: 1]


4. PANE SHORTCUTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ctrl+B then %                       Split window vertically[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then "                       Split window horizontally[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then <Arrow Keys>            Navigate between panes (Left / Right / Up / Down)[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then O                       Switch to next pane[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then X                       Close current pane[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then Z                       Toggle zoom on active pane[cite: 1]
Ctrl+B then Q                       Display pane numbers[cite: 1]


5. SCROLL & COPY MODE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ctrl+B then [                       Enter scroll / copy mode[cite: 1]
Up / Down / PageUp / PageDown       Scroll through output history[cite: 1]
Q                                   Exit scroll mode[cite: 1]
